# SKY-FLICKER: everything in front of the clouds flickers at moments under a STILL camera (owner, FIELD_Barn and
# Bistro: "листва все еще моментами мерцает", "и не только листва, все что на фоне облаков").
# Cause (VolumetricCloudRenderer.cpp, CloudTemporalResolve.shader): the cloud march traced through the JITTERED
# inverse (TAA1-VIEW e1f461f31) while its temporal resolve reprojects through the UNJITTERED previous matrix, so at
# a still camera every history read landed up to a quarter half-res texel off, the bilinear history guide mixed a
# leaf's distance with the sky's, the 2 km disocclusion test dropped the history along every silhouette on most
# jitter frames, and a fresh / edge-mixed trace showed there instead; and a footprint wholly covered by a leaf on
# one jitter frame and open on the next swung its trace between "clear at the leaf" and "cloud at the far plane".
# Fix: unjittered cloud view (UE HackRemoveTemporalAAProjectionJitter) + geometry in front of the layer cuts nothing
# (Common/CloudSceneDepth.glslh, CloudFootprintOccluded).
# Same project line and still air as FPS-FIELD-BARN (default machine settings, no machine.json overrides); the view
# is FOLIAGE-CLOUD-FLICKER's: grass blades, canopy and fence edges over the cloud layer. 300 warm frames, then
# eight shots on eight consecutive frames.
# MEASURE (lead, pixel diff, not thumbnails): edge band = pixels within 8 px of an object/sky boundary (scene depth
# 0 on one side; or, from the frames alone, |Sobel| of 8_h's luma above 0.1 dilated by 8 px). For k = 2..8 the
# mean over the band of |frame k - frame k-1| (all channels, /255): record it on the BEFORE build (dev 94a6eea4b)
# and on task/SKY-FLICKER.
# SKY-FLICKER-2: the cloud itself flickered over the whole sky, not only at edges. The march's start offset was a
# white hash per frame and the resolve kept 75 % of every new trace, so each half-res pixel jumped by one fresh
# realization of the dither every fourth frame; the TAA's variance clip (3x3 of a smooth upsample) let the jump
# through. Fix: spatio-temporal low-discrepancy start offset (IGN x 2x2 rank x golden ratio per trace, UE
# BlueNoiseScalar), and on a still history the owned trace blends at 1-(1-0.04)^4 = 0.15 (the TAA's own time
# constant) while a not-owned pixel keeps the history whole with its front (UE ReprojRGBA / ReprojDepthData).
# MEASURE (lead): sky mean = mean |frame k - frame k-1| over every pixel with scene depth 0 (or, from the frames,
# luma above the 1_a sky's 5th percentile outside the edge band); record it on task/SKY-FLICKER 7ad033aec and
# on task/SKY-FLICKER-2, for k = 2..8. Brightness: the sky's SIGNED mean luma of 8_h within 1/255 of the same
# frame on task/SKY-FLICKER (the new value is an average of the same dither, so a shift would be a defect).
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/FIELD_Barn.desce --gpu-profile
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,40,2500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,0.25,-1
Дано set 8180000000000004 WindSourceData.Speed 0
Когда frames 300
Когда profile-dump
Тогда [log] the [Profiler] per-pass table carries "Clouds: March"; its GPU ms is not above the task/SKY-FLICKER 7ad033aec run of this scenario
Тогда-вид 1_a still camera at 0.4 m looking up: grass blades, canopy and fence edges over the clouds, crisp; editor.log 0 VUID
Тогда-вид 2_b the next frame: in the 8 px band around every object/sky edge the mean |2_b - 1_a| <= 1/255; over the whole cloudy sky (not only the band) the mean |2_b - 1_a| below the task/SKY-FLICKER 7ad033aec value
Тогда-вид 3_c the next frame: band mean |3_c - 2_b| <= 1/255
Тогда-вид 4_d the next frame: band mean |4_d - 3_c| <= 1/255
Тогда-вид 5_e the next frame: band mean |5_e - 4_d| <= 1/255
Тогда-вид 6_f the next frame: band mean |6_f - 5_e| <= 1/255
Тогда-вид 7_g the next frame: band mean |7_g - 6_f| <= 1/255
Тогда-вид 8_h the next frame: band mean |8_h - 7_g| <= 1/255; the clouds behind the blades the same shape and brightness as in 1_a (no cloud lost or gained at any edge, no new banding in the cloud bodies); editor.log 0 VUID
